    "created_at": "2017-10-11T08:31:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-11T08:31:56Z",
    "body": "> Lars could you explain the actual use-case, so that we understand why this is useful?\r\n\r\nIn my own case, I have a series of devices that I want to be 'available' or not on selection (connected to a hub).\r\n\r\nOutside this scope, there could easily be the case that users of multiple machines (e.g. cash registers, school computers, etc.) would like to have only one particular piece of hardware paired/attached at a time or possibly wanted to 'decommission' some broken hardware, not have the old one 'paired' anymore, etc.. \r\n\r\nI know it can be done in the browser UI - but it took me a minute to find the place (together with other permissions - so that speaks against it of course - unless it should be considered to add 'forget' functionality to geolocation, user media, etc.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
